WEBVTT

00:01:14.001 --> 00:01:15.402
And the King said...

00:01:15.402 --> 00:01:17.237
Strange Tale of Lasagna
And the King said...

00:01:17.237 --> 00:01:19.773
Strange Tale of Lasagna
"Give the child to this woman...

00:01:19.773 --> 00:01:22.571
...for she is its true mother."

00:01:23.777 --> 00:01:26.541
And the people saw he
was full of wisdom.

00:01:27.181 --> 00:01:30.480
Injustice will lose its power
and justice will bring serenity.

00:01:31.585 --> 00:01:36.682
Here lies Marco Belnine.
May his soul rest in peace.

00:01:37.191 --> 00:01:38.123
Amen.

00:01:38.926 --> 00:01:40.052
Amen.

00:01:44.098 --> 00:01:47.261
Florence, Italy

00:01:59.813 --> 00:02:02.646
Italian cars sure have character.

00:02:04.485 --> 00:02:05.652
Oh?

00:02:05.652 --> 00:02:07.779
The end of the Renaissance?

00:02:08.088 --> 00:02:11.125
A perfect example of a
prosperous Florentine family.

00:02:11.125 --> 00:02:13.389
Well, Signore Keaton.

00:02:13.794 --> 00:02:16.463
I have no intention of letting
that gold digger...

00:02:16.463 --> 00:02:18.158
...take away my
beautiful granddaughter.

00:02:18.599 --> 00:02:19.293
Right.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.902
But, Signora Belnine...

00:02:21.902 --> 00:02:25.272
...the mother has legal rights
in this case, and...

00:02:25.272 --> 00:02:26.907
Laws mean nothing!

00:02:26.907 --> 00:02:27.896
Right...

00:02:28.108 --> 00:02:30.744
She started going after another man...

00:02:30.744 --> 00:02:33.547
...soon after my son was laid
in his final resting place.

00:02:33.547 --> 00:02:34.515
Well, that's...

00:02:34.515 --> 00:02:37.109
She needs a good environment.

00:02:37.551 --> 00:02:41.248
I've arranged the best environment
for a child to grow up in.

00:02:42.656 --> 00:02:45.993
I'd like to confirm what Flora
feels about all this.

00:02:45.993 --> 00:02:47.795
Of course...

00:02:47.795 --> 00:02:51.532
...she doesn't want to go
with that heartless woman.

00:02:51.532 --> 00:02:53.567
Yes, but...

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.169
Franco.

00:02:55.169 --> 00:02:57.103
This man is leaving now.

00:03:07.114 --> 00:03:09.514
It certainly is a beautiful house.

00:03:10.484 --> 00:03:12.850
It's your last chance to see it.

00:03:13.187 --> 00:03:15.923
Is Miss Flora's bedroom
on the third floor?

00:03:15.923 --> 00:03:17.724
Open your eyes.

00:03:17.724 --> 00:03:19.960
There're only two floors.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.157
Her room's just over there
at the top corner.

00:03:23.564 --> 00:03:24.326
Really?

00:03:25.065 --> 00:03:26.532
You were leaving.

00:03:27.301 --> 00:03:28.996
Might as well.

00:03:44.985 --> 00:03:47.317
My mother-in-law is
a horrible woman.

00:03:47.888 --> 00:03:49.189
She was born into a wealthy...

00:03:49.189 --> 00:03:50.858
Marseilles, France
...and influential family in Italy.

00:03:50.858 --> 00:03:52.893
Marseilles, France
She gets everything she wants.

00:03:52.893 --> 00:03:53.518
She gets everything she wants.

00:03:54.828 --> 00:03:58.696
And now she's trying to
take away my daughter.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.902
While Marco was alive...

00:04:01.902 --> 00:04:04.234
...she showed no interest in her.

00:04:04.638 --> 00:04:06.731
But as soon as he died...

00:04:07.941 --> 00:04:09.841
I was careless, too.

00:04:10.644 --> 00:04:14.876
I shouldn't have let Flora go there
by herself for Christmas holidays.

00:04:16.984 --> 00:04:17.916
Excuse me.

00:04:20.888 --> 00:04:21.946
Who is it?

00:04:22.389 --> 00:04:23.223
It's me.

00:04:23.223 --> 00:04:24.121
Alan!

00:04:25.225 --> 00:04:26.093
Alan.

00:04:26.093 --> 00:04:27.561
It's over between us.

00:04:27.561 --> 00:04:30.257
I want to help. Why can't we talk?

00:04:31.598 --> 00:04:33.667
I can't. Just leave.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:34.463
Please.

00:04:35.202 --> 00:04:36.370
I see.

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.462
Okay, I understand.

00:04:40.641 --> 00:04:41.699
Is that it?

00:04:43.477 --> 00:04:45.775
Yes. It's all over.

00:04:52.452 --> 00:04:55.819
All I need is Flora right now.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:00.217
My only hope is to live
with my daughter.

00:05:17.177 --> 00:05:19.042
Oh, boy...

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:27.688
Are you Flora?

00:05:27.688 --> 00:05:30.390
You're the detective that
my mama sent, aren't you?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:31.448
Let's go now.

00:05:31.925 --> 00:05:33.449
Does your grandma know about this?

00:05:34.561 --> 00:05:36.426
I hate her.

00:05:39.166 --> 00:05:41.735
Don't you think
we should get going?

00:05:41.735 --> 00:05:42.336
Huh?

00:05:42.336 --> 00:05:43.303
Franco!

00:05:44.304 --> 00:05:45.328
Franco!

00:05:47.107 --> 00:05:49.943
Franco used to be a boxer.

00:05:49.943 --> 00:05:51.808
Do you know how to box?

00:05:52.012 --> 00:05:52.910
L-Let's go.

00:06:02.923 --> 00:06:03.855
Got it.

00:06:25.645 --> 00:06:26.613
Oh, hot!

00:06:26.613 --> 00:06:27.580
Hot, hot!

00:06:28.248 --> 00:06:31.284
Well, I'm cooking dinner
at the moment.

00:06:31.284 --> 00:06:32.986
That's not important!

00:06:32.986 --> 00:06:35.055
You cancelled classes last week,
and then again this week!

00:06:35.055 --> 00:06:36.523
We've had enough of this!

00:06:36.523 --> 00:06:38.548
What on earth are you up to?!

00:06:38.825 --> 00:06:39.259
Ouch.

00:06:39.259 --> 00:06:41.728
Mr. Keaton, are you there?!

00:06:41.728 --> 00:06:43.864
I'll be sure to attend next week.

00:06:43.864 --> 00:06:45.331
Hello?!

00:06:46.933 --> 00:06:48.668
Mr. Keaton?! Hello?!

00:06:48.668 --> 00:06:49.862
Mr. Keaton?!

00:06:50.604 --> 00:06:51.571
What's going on?

00:06:51.571 --> 00:06:53.766
Well, uh...

00:06:54.274 --> 00:06:56.410
I forgot the mozzarella cheese.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.436
I won't be able to make
lasagna without that.

00:06:59.613 --> 00:07:00.739
I'll go buy some.

00:07:01.181 --> 00:07:02.170
Lasagna?

00:07:02.649 --> 00:07:04.879
Yes. Lasagna alla Milano.

00:07:06.086 --> 00:07:07.951
Let's eat out.

00:07:08.321 --> 00:07:10.312
I really hate lasagna.

00:07:10.957 --> 00:07:11.719
Huh?

00:07:12.092 --> 00:07:13.787
Right, then...

00:07:17.798 --> 00:07:20.834
Papa promised me that
when I get older...

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:25.134
...he would take me to a
nice restaurant like this.

00:07:26.339 --> 00:07:29.934
Papa was a great dancer
and he made the best lasagna.

00:07:30.077 --> 00:07:32.545
Then, why don't you like lasagna?

00:07:45.692 --> 00:07:47.819
You know, you're actually
kind of cute.

00:07:49.262 --> 00:07:50.464
How old are you?

00:07:50.464 --> 00:07:52.193
Oh, uh...

00:07:52.466 --> 00:07:54.195
Wait, let me guess.

00:07:54.634 --> 00:07:57.194
I bet you look younger
than you are.

00:07:58.572 --> 00:07:59.698
Around 50?

00:08:01.341 --> 00:08:04.174
Close, compared to you.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.481
Lovely.

00:08:12.586 --> 00:08:15.646
I was eight when I
went to my first party.

00:08:16.356 --> 00:08:18.017
It was wonderful.

00:08:18.625 --> 00:08:22.755
Mama even let me stay up
until 10 o'clock at night.

00:08:23.196 --> 00:08:24.531
I danced with Papa.

00:08:24.531 --> 00:08:26.726
I was wearing a white dress
that night.

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:38.937
Hey, why don't we dance?

00:08:40.647 --> 00:08:42.342
I'm not a good dancer.

00:08:45.752 --> 00:08:46.820
You were lying.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:49.482
You didn't want to dance
with a little girl, right?

00:08:49.723 --> 00:08:52.392
No, I'm telling the truth.
I can't dance.

00:08:52.392 --> 00:08:54.826
It's not good manners
to turn down a lady.

00:08:58.165 --> 00:09:00.700
Flora, let's forget about the car.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:01.325
Huh?

00:09:24.824 --> 00:09:26.126
One child and one adult.

00:09:26.126 --> 00:09:27.423
To the end of the line.

00:09:29.629 --> 00:09:31.119
That would be Pisa.

00:09:37.837 --> 00:09:40.740
I thought detectives were
supposed to be cool.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:44.301
I'd rather dance than get
involved in rough stuff.

00:09:57.791 --> 00:10:00.282
Why'd you go to
your grandmother's?

00:10:00.927 --> 00:10:03.020
I wanted to punish my mama.

00:10:04.364 --> 00:10:06.025
You're mad at your mother?

00:10:06.132 --> 00:10:07.599
But I hate Grandmother.

00:10:08.802 --> 00:10:11.930
She's convinced that Papa died
because of Mama.

00:10:12.105 --> 00:10:14.972
So she's been using me
for revenge.

00:10:15.308 --> 00:10:17.208
She doesn't even like me.

00:10:19.012 --> 00:10:20.206
Are you married?

00:10:20.513 --> 00:10:21.605
Uh, no...

00:10:22.082 --> 00:10:22.980
Right now.

00:10:23.617 --> 00:10:24.845
I'm divorced.

00:10:26.519 --> 00:10:28.680
So, you must be lonely as well.

00:10:30.223 --> 00:10:33.317
But you have both your
mother and grandmother.

00:10:34.561 --> 00:10:35.994
Mr. Keaton?

00:10:37.063 --> 00:10:39.199
Do you still think about...

00:10:39.199 --> 00:10:41.099
...your ex-wife?

00:10:44.304 --> 00:10:45.100
Sometimes.

00:10:45.438 --> 00:10:46.706
I thought so.

00:10:46.706 --> 00:10:48.408
Once you love someone...

00:10:48.408 --> 00:10:51.809
...you can't forget about them,
even if they're gone.

00:10:52.979 --> 00:10:54.571
I wonder.

00:10:55.148 --> 00:10:55.682
Hey.

00:10:55.682 --> 00:10:58.150
How about we run away together?

00:10:58.718 --> 00:11:02.355
My father's insurance money
is going to come to me.

00:11:02.355 --> 00:11:04.124
I'm rich, you know.

00:11:04.124 --> 00:11:05.216
I know.

00:11:05.558 --> 00:11:07.719
We can tell people that
I'm your daughter.

00:11:08.061 --> 00:11:09.462
You're very sweet.

00:11:09.462 --> 00:11:10.827
But I already have a daughter.

00:11:12.032 --> 00:11:13.329
I see.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:14.868
It won't work, then...

00:11:14.868 --> 00:11:16.460
...if you already have a daughter.

00:11:38.725 --> 00:11:39.384
What is it?

00:11:41.428 --> 00:11:43.362
I had a scary dream.

00:11:45.732 --> 00:11:49.759
Papa was inside his car,
falling off a cliff.

00:11:51.538 --> 00:11:54.598
I was sitting in the car, too.

00:11:55.975 --> 00:12:00.002
And my mama was pushing
the car over the cliff...

00:12:01.014 --> 00:12:04.177
...and she was laughing.

00:12:08.621 --> 00:12:11.191
Your mother wouldn't
do such a thing.

00:12:11.191 --> 00:12:15.095
Your father was drunk
and fell asleep at the wheel.

00:12:15.095 --> 00:12:16.722
That's why he went over the cliff.

00:12:18.031 --> 00:12:20.261
I investigated the case.

00:12:22.035 --> 00:12:23.866
I know about that.

00:12:24.304 --> 00:12:26.238
It doesn't matter anyway.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:30.977
Only a year has gone by since
my papa passed away and...

00:12:30.977 --> 00:12:33.969
...mama is already trying to
marry another man called Alan.

00:12:35.982 --> 00:12:37.183
Don't you think that's terrible?

00:12:37.183 --> 00:12:39.811
I mean, Papa just died!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.618
I'm the only one who
truly loved him...

00:12:44.224 --> 00:12:46.055
...and now I'm all alone.

00:12:47.026 --> 00:12:49.824
I don't want to live anymore.

00:12:52.665 --> 00:12:54.234
If you were to die now...

00:12:54.234 --> 00:12:58.500
...then who would be around
to listen to my ultimate joke?

00:12:59.906 --> 00:13:01.305
Ultimate joke?

00:13:01.641 --> 00:13:02.409
Yes.

00:13:02.409 --> 00:13:03.637
It's a great one.

00:13:04.911 --> 00:13:07.046
My old friend from college...

00:13:07.046 --> 00:13:09.844
...fled to the Soviet Union
after hearing it.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:14.817
You doubt me?

00:13:15.422 --> 00:13:17.083
You think I'm a liar.

00:13:21.961 --> 00:13:23.019
Flora.

00:13:23.263 --> 00:13:26.960
Your mother told me she
isn't going to marry Alan.

00:13:28.168 --> 00:13:28.896
No way.

00:13:29.803 --> 00:13:33.864
Now, I think you agreed
I wasn't a liar?

00:13:35.442 --> 00:13:37.177
When someone's in love...

00:13:37.177 --> 00:13:39.512
...it takes a lot of courage...

00:13:39.512 --> 00:13:43.249
...for that person to give up
that part of her life...

00:13:43.249 --> 00:13:45.479
...for somebody else.

00:13:46.252 --> 00:13:49.278
Even if it's for her own child.

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:53.056
Your mother won't abandon you.

00:13:53.593 --> 00:13:56.027
She's waiting at
home for you.

00:13:56.463 --> 00:13:57.794
All by herself.

00:14:03.503 --> 00:14:05.232
Think you'll have bad dreams?

00:14:11.344 --> 00:14:12.606
Mr. Keaton?

00:14:13.947 --> 00:14:15.539
Leave the lights on.

00:14:15.949 --> 00:14:17.314
The door's open, too.

00:14:18.318 --> 00:14:22.379
Mr. Keaton, won't you tell me
your ultimate joke?

00:14:23.223 --> 00:14:25.282
Not till we reach Marseilles.

00:15:14.741 --> 00:15:15.901
It's yummy!

00:15:20.013 --> 00:15:21.514
Do you like linguini?

00:15:21.514 --> 00:15:22.215
Yes.

00:15:22.215 --> 00:15:23.383
So, you like pasta?

00:15:23.383 --> 00:15:24.680
I love it.

00:15:25.485 --> 00:15:28.388
Then, why don't you like lasagna?

00:15:28.388 --> 00:15:31.915
It means "baked dish"
and it's a pasta.

00:15:34.994 --> 00:15:35.892
Flora...

00:15:42.001 --> 00:15:44.270
You're not hurt, are you?

00:15:44.270 --> 00:15:45.259
Grandmother.

00:15:46.172 --> 00:15:47.707
Signore Keaton.

00:15:47.707 --> 00:15:49.309
What is all this about?

00:15:49.309 --> 00:15:51.539
Kidnapping my granddaughter.

00:15:52.278 --> 00:15:53.472
You're wrong, Grandmother!

00:15:53.913 --> 00:15:54.881
Flora.

00:15:54.881 --> 00:15:57.050
You've been fooled all along.

00:15:57.050 --> 00:15:58.117
Well, Madam.

00:15:58.117 --> 00:16:00.386
He's the kidnapper, all right.

00:16:00.386 --> 00:16:02.149
It's time to teach him a lesson.

00:16:02.555 --> 00:16:05.046
How unfortunate for you,
Signore Keaton.

00:16:15.668 --> 00:16:17.898
What?
Something wrong with my face?

00:16:18.504 --> 00:16:20.039
Did you have some lasagna?

00:16:20.039 --> 00:16:22.030
There's cheese on your chin.

00:16:36.756 --> 00:16:38.224
Signore Keaton...

00:16:38.224 --> 00:16:40.419
How much do you want?

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:42.122
What do you mean?

00:16:42.996 --> 00:16:46.261
Your fee for babysitting
my granddaughter.

00:16:46.466 --> 00:16:49.128
Or would you rather be
charged with kidnapping?

00:16:49.369 --> 00:16:50.503
Grandmother!

00:16:50.503 --> 00:16:52.334
We're going home, Flora.

00:16:53.706 --> 00:16:56.142
I didn't mention this to you before.

00:16:56.142 --> 00:16:58.411
But while your poor father
was still alive...

00:16:58.411 --> 00:17:00.777
...your own mother was
seeing another man.

00:17:02.949 --> 00:17:06.953
Going to live with that woman
isn't going to do you any good.

00:17:06.953 --> 00:17:07.885
Now, Flora.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:11.352
I knew that.

00:17:13.459 --> 00:17:14.323
Flora...

00:17:15.128 --> 00:17:17.028
I've known about everything.

00:17:17.597 --> 00:17:20.122
Since the night at that
party when I was eight.

00:17:21.801 --> 00:17:24.895
Flora seemed to have a great time.

00:17:25.271 --> 00:17:26.101
Anna.

00:17:26.539 --> 00:17:28.302
I want to talk to you about
our future.

00:17:29.108 --> 00:17:31.911
If you're concerned about Flora,
I'll take care of her.

00:17:31.911 --> 00:17:34.778
Alan, it wouldn't be fair to her.

00:17:35.415 --> 00:17:38.418
Flora loves Marco.

00:17:38.418 --> 00:17:39.715
I need more time.

00:17:40.186 --> 00:17:41.454
That scoundrel.

00:17:41.454 --> 00:17:42.751
Alan, please don't.

00:17:43.089 --> 00:17:45.958
I bet he's drunk again right now...

00:17:45.958 --> 00:17:48.449
...and he's in bed with
some other woman.

00:17:52.865 --> 00:17:56.926
Your kiss tastes like the
lasagna we had tonight.

00:17:57.603 --> 00:17:59.662
Like the lasagna we had tonight...

00:18:01.841 --> 00:18:03.776
My poor Marco.

00:18:03.776 --> 00:18:06.079
Betrayed by that awful woman.

00:18:06.079 --> 00:18:07.944
Don't talk badly about my mama!

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:11.947
Flora...

00:18:13.386 --> 00:18:17.156
It's Papa's fault because
he made Mama go to Alan.

00:18:17.156 --> 00:18:18.858
What are you saying?
Marco was...

00:18:18.858 --> 00:18:21.986
He was always nice
when he was around me.

00:18:22.528 --> 00:18:24.189
But he was mean to Mama.

00:18:25.331 --> 00:18:27.633
He was always getting drunk.

00:18:27.633 --> 00:18:29.260
Then, he would hit her.

00:18:29.569 --> 00:18:32.037
He flirted with other women.

00:18:32.505 --> 00:18:34.632
I'm sure you know all about that.

00:18:35.775 --> 00:18:37.744
I'm going back to my mama.

00:18:37.744 --> 00:18:40.304
You can't.
I won't allow it.

00:18:40.613 --> 00:18:43.639
I loved Papa.

00:18:43.983 --> 00:18:45.883
And you, too.

00:18:46.619 --> 00:18:49.952
But I also love my mama, too.

00:18:58.197 --> 00:18:59.664
All right.

00:19:01.567 --> 00:19:05.025
A girl like you can't be
my son's daughter.

00:19:05.538 --> 00:19:07.062
You're that woman's child.

00:19:08.207 --> 00:19:08.935
Franco!

00:19:14.914 --> 00:19:16.347
Madam...!

00:19:17.216 --> 00:19:18.274
Grandmother!

00:19:19.118 --> 00:19:21.916
Can I visit you next Christmas?

00:19:23.122 --> 00:19:24.487
Do as you please.

00:19:38.037 --> 00:19:39.698
Mr. Keaton?

00:19:40.473 --> 00:19:44.000
We'll be in Marseilles
soon after we cross the border.

00:19:45.945 --> 00:19:46.934
That's right.

00:19:48.781 --> 00:19:52.308
A man got really angry in
a bar for being called bear.

00:19:53.653 --> 00:19:56.322
He went on a rampage in the bar...

00:19:56.322 --> 00:19:58.813
...and after a struggle,
he was finally arrested.

00:20:02.228 --> 00:20:06.399
Then he told the officer that
he forgot his fur...

00:20:06.399 --> 00:20:08.094
...and that he really was a bear.

00:20:08.568 --> 00:20:13.062
He claimed that a little roughness
from a bear shouldn't be a crime.

00:20:15.541 --> 00:20:17.304
Then, the officer said...

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.813
"You weren't arrested because
you were violent."

00:20:20.813 --> 00:20:23.873
"You're under arrest for
indecent exposure."

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:26.215
To that, the man said...

00:20:26.652 --> 00:20:28.813
"But I'm clean."

00:20:31.757 --> 00:20:33.292
Mr. Keaton.

00:20:33.292 --> 00:20:35.294
When I get older...

00:20:35.294 --> 00:20:38.388
...will you dance with me then?

00:20:48.841 --> 00:20:50.042
My lady.

00:20:50.042 --> 00:20:51.873
Can I have this dance?

00:20:53.546 --> 00:20:55.639
It's a beautiful moonlit evening.

00:20:56.115 --> 00:20:58.310
But people are watching.

00:20:58.618 --> 00:21:02.054
And you really don't want to
dance with a child, do you?

00:21:02.054 --> 00:21:03.189
No.

00:21:03.189 --> 00:21:04.383
You're different now.

00:21:05.758 --> 00:21:08.488
You're a charming lady now.

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:29.548
Mr. Keaton...

00:21:29.548 --> 00:21:31.140
You are a liar, after all.

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:32.144
Oh?

00:21:32.752 --> 00:21:35.488
It turns out you're a good dancer.

00:21:35.488 --> 00:21:39.948
But your ultimate joke
really wasn't funny at all.

00:21:53.205 --> 00:22:03.883
In a dream I had,
I noticed your distant, faint voice

00:22:03.883 --> 00:22:11.289
A scene so familiar
playing out in reality

00:22:11.991 --> 00:22:15.483
In my consciousness

00:22:16.195 --> 00:22:24.236
The sky I was searching for
brings forth a gentleness

00:22:24.236 --> 00:22:27.967
Time will give me the answer

00:22:34.547 --> 00:22:40.052
In the blank scene before me

00:22:40.052 --> 00:22:46.058
I walk as the wind blows

00:22:46.058 --> 00:22:53.332
I just want to touch it
with my own hands

00:22:53.332 --> 00:22:59.999
As the wind blows against me

00:23:07.446 --> 00:23:08.948
The old man said...

00:23:08.948 --> 00:23:11.951
"Life is simply no fun
without thrills."

00:23:11.951 --> 00:23:13.753
The old man laughed...

00:23:13.753 --> 00:23:15.812
"Let's enjoy this danger."

00:23:16.222 --> 00:23:18.491
The old man cursed...

00:23:18.491 --> 00:23:21.892
"The snow will even
hide the fresh blood."

00:23:22.094 --> 00:23:23.662
Then the old man revealed...

00:23:23.662 --> 00:23:26.766
"Somewhere in this world
there is a secret treasure."

00:23:26.766 --> 00:23:28.934
Then the old man cried out...

00:23:28.934 --> 00:23:29.935
Immortal Man

00:23:29.935 --> 00:23:32.004
Immortal Man
Next time... Immortal Man

00:23:32.004 --> 00:23:32.993
Immortal Man
